message: "Si vous utilisez ce travail dans une publication, veuillez le citer ainsi :"
title: "RATISS V10 AEON PRIME: A Physical Complexity Audit Framework for the P vs NP Problem"
authors:
  - family-names: Evina
    given-names: Jonathan
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0000-4092-5313
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
  - family-names: "Johnking0"
    given-names: ""
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
abstract: |
  The RATISS V10 AEON PRIME ecosystem maps computational complexity to fundamental physical
  bounds (Margolus-Levitin, Landauer, Zurek decoherence, Bekenstein bound, Special Relativity)
  and proposes three physically grounded challenges (UPCF, CEOE, RPS) as replacements for
  the classical P vs NP formulation of the Clay Mathematics Institute.
keywords:
  - P vs NP
  - Physical Complexity
  - Margolus-Levitin Theorem
  - Landauer Principle
  - Quantum Decoherence
  - Bekenstein Bound
  - Computational Physics
  - Complexity Theory
